-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### B3. Requirement ID 003
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This requirement calls for careful interpretation. At first glance, it seems almost identical to the previous one, but there are two key differences:
-- MAGIC - privileges should be scoped to the `traffic` schema
-- MAGIC - privileges should be limited to reading and writing tables
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC We can still leverage privilege inheritance to achieve this by applying privileges at the schema level, but they cannot be as extensive as the previous example.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC In this case, we need:
-- MAGIC - `USE CATALOG` on the containing catalog
-- MAGIC - `USE SCHEMA` on the containing schema
-- MAGIC - `SELECT` and `MODIFY` also on the schema, to read/write all tables in the schema
-- MAGIC
