GRANT USE CATALOG ON CATALOG `law_prd` TO `account users`;
GRANT USE SCHEMA,SELECT ON SCHEMA `law_prd`.`traffic` TO `account users`;

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## C. Implementing ABAC
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC As discussed in a previous lessons, there is a systemic workflow for ABAC planning, In this section, we put these steps into motion implementing the final requirement for our dataset governance requirements.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Policies provide for a lot of flexibility for managing data access based on attributes (tags). In a full-fledged migration, the design process will output custom governed tags that can be used for implementing enhanced complex governance policies. But in this simplified example, we will restrict our example policies to:
-- MAGIC - using the system-provided data classification tags
-- MAGIC - implementing a policy that redacts classified data from public consumption

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### C1. Discover/Classify Data
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC In this step, we review the tables in the dataset and tag it using system-provided classification tags. The process could be further enhanced to include customer governed tags, however to keep thing simple we will restrict this example to using the system-provided tags.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Review the `driver_dim` table within the dataset. Apply system governed tags to the columns as appropriate: 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <style>
-- MAGIC table{
-- MAGIC   border-collapse: separate;
-- MAGIC   border-spacing: 0;
-- MAGIC   width: auto;
-- MAGIC   max-width: 100%;
-- MAGIC   margin: 16px 0;
-- MAGIC   float: none;
-- MAGIC   clear: both;
-- MAGIC   display: table;
-- MAGIC   font-size: 0.95em;
-- MAGIC   line-height: 1.35;
-- MAGIC   background: #ffffff;
-- MAGIC   border-radius: 8px;
-- MAGIC   overflow: hidden;
-- MAGIC   box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #303F47;
-- MAGIC   margin-left: 2px !important;
-- MAGIC   margin-right: 0px !important;
-- MAGIC   box-sizing: border-box !important;
-- MAGIC }
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC thead th{
-- MAGIC   background: #DADADA;
-- MAGIC   color: #1B3139;
-- MAGIC   font-weight: 600;
-- MAGIC   text-align: left;
-- MAGIC   padding: 10px 12px;
-- MAGIC }
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC tbody td{
-- MAGIC   padding: 10px 12px;
-- MAGIC   border-top: 1px solid #DCE0E2;
-- MAGIC }
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC tbody tr:nth-child(odd){
-- MAGIC   background: #FFFFFF !important;
-- MAGIC }
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC tbody tr:nth-child(even){
-- MAGIC   background: #F5F3F2 !important;
-- MAGIC }
-- MAGIC </style>
-- MAGIC <table>
-- MAGIC   <thead>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <th>Column</th>
-- MAGIC       <th>Tag</th>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC   </thead>
-- MAGIC   <tbody>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td>name</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>class.name</td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td>license_number</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>class.us_driver_license</td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td>address</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>class.location</td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td>phone_number</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>class.phone_number</td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC   </tbody>
-- MAGIC </table>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This can be done in Catalog Explorer (by clicking **Add tags** in the **Tags** column), or by executing a SQL statement as follows (configured for the `name` column):
-- MAGIC <div class="code-block" data-language="sql">
-- MAGIC ALTER TABLE `law_prd`.`traffic`.`driver_dim` ALTER COLUMN `name` SET TAGS ('class.name');
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC   <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC   <div>
-- MAGIC     The statement shown only tags a single column; it would have to be repeated for each tagging pair.
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC <link href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/themes/prism.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
-- MAGIC <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/prism.min.js"></script>
-- MAGIC <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/prism/1.29.0/components/prism-sql.min.js"></script>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <script>
-- MAGIC (function() {
-- MAGIC     document.querySelectorAll('.code-block').forEach(function(block) {
-- MAGIC         if (block.getAttribute('data-processed')) return;
-- MAGIC         block.setAttribute('data-processed', 'true');
-- MAGIC         var lang = block.getAttribute('data-language') || 'sql';
-- MAGIC         var code = block.textContent.trim();
-- MAGIC         var id = 'code-' + Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);
-- MAGIC         block.innerHTML = 
-- MAGIC             '<div style="position:relative;margin:16px 0;">' +
-- MAGIC                 '<button class="copy-btn" style="position:absolute;top:8px;right:8px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:12px;background:#ddd;color:#333;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:4px;cursor:pointer;z-index:10;">Copy</button>' +
-- MAGIC                 '<pre style="background:#f8f8f8;border-radius:8px;padding:16px;padding-top:40px;overflow-x:auto;margin:0;border:1px solid #e0e0e0;"><code id="' + id + '" class="language-' + lang + '" style="font-family:Consolas,Monaco,monospace;font-size:14px;"></code></pre>' +
-- MAGIC             '</div>';
-- MAGIC         var codeEl = document.getElementById(id);
-- MAGIC         codeEl.textContent = code;
-- MAGIC         Prism.highlightElement(codeEl);
-- MAGIC         block.querySelector('.copy-btn').onclick = function() {
