-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### C5. Define Governed Tags
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Governed tags will likely be instrumental in any deployment, as they can allow you to configure custom tags with values, which can also be applied in the ABAC policies we've seen.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC In this example, we focus on a simple example: adding a `sensitivity` tag, provided as part of the example starter taxonomy provided earlier in this material.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       In order to add governed tags, you must be an account or workspace admin, or have been granted the <code>CREATE</code> privilege at the account level.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. In the catalog explorer, select **Govern &gt; Governed Tags**.
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Create governed tag**
-- MAGIC 1. Specify a tag key (for example *sensitivity*).
-- MAGIC 1. Click **Create**.
-- MAGIC 1. In the **Policy Definition** tab, click **Add value**.
-- MAGIC 1. Enter three values (*low*, *medium*, and *high*) and click **Add**.

